{
  "id": "he-6",
  "lang": "he",
  "title": "Nouns: masculine, feminine, plural",
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": "hear",
      "intro": "Every Hebrew noun is masculine or feminine, and its ending changes when there is more than one. Listen for -im, -ot and -ayim.",
      "cards": [
        { "type": "scene", "picture": "🐎", "text": "סוּס", "say": "sus", "en": "a horse" },
        { "type": "scene", "picture": "🐎🐎🐎", "text": "סוּסִים", "say": "su-SIM", "en": "horses" },
        { "type": "scene", "picture": "👩", "text": "אִשָּׁה", "say": "i-SHAH", "en": "a woman" },
        { "type": "scene", "picture": "👩‍👩‍👧", "text": "נָשִׁים", "say": "na-SHIM", "en": "women: an irregular plural" },
        { "type": "scene", "picture": "👀", "text": "עֵינַיִם", "say": "ei-NA-yim", "en": "(a pair of) eyes" },
        { "type": "scene", "picture": "📅", "text": "יָמִים", "say": "ya-MIM", "en": "days" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "notice",
      "cards": [
        {
          "type": "explain",
          "title": "Masculine and feminine",
          "body": [
            "Masculine nouns have no special ending: סוּס, דָּבָר. Feminine nouns usually end in ָה or ת: מִצְוָה (commandment), בַּת (daughter).",
            "Gender is part of the word, not always its meaning. אֶרֶץ (land) and עִיר (city) are feminine without the ending, so learn each noun's gender as you go."
          ],
          "table": {
            "head": ["", "one", "more than one"],
            "rows": [
              ["masculine", "דָּבָר", "דְּבָרִים"],
              ["feminine", "מִצְוָה", "מִצְוֹת"],
              ["a pair", "עַיִן", "עֵינַיִם"]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "explain",
          "title": "The plural endings",
          "body": [
            "Masculine plural: -ִים (-im). Feminine plural: -וֹת (-ot), replacing the ָה. Things that come in pairs, like eyes, hands and feet, use -ַיִם (-ayim), the dual.",
            "Adding an ending often changes the vowels near the front, because the stress moves to the end: דָּבָר becomes דְּבָרִים, מֶלֶךְ becomes מְלָכִים.",
            "A few common nouns are irregular, and some take the “wrong” ending: אִישׁ, men, is אֲנָשִׁים; אָב, father, is אָבוֹת; שָׁנָה, year, is שָׁנִים."
          ],
          "examples": [
            { "t": "מְלָכִים", "say": "me-la-KHIM", "en": "kings" },
            { "t": "אֲנָשִׁים", "say": "a-na-SHIM", "en": "men" },
            { "t": "אָבוֹת", "say": "a-VOT", "en": "fathers" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "practise",
      "cards": [
        {
          "type": "choose",
          "prompt": "What does סוּסִים mean?",
          "options": ["horses", "a horse", "a mare", "two horses"],
          "answer": 0,
          "explain": "-ִים is the masculine plural ending: horses."
        },
        {
          "type": "choose",
          "prompt": "Which of these is feminine?",
          "options": ["מִצְוָה", "סוּס", "דָּבָר", "יוֹם"],
          "answer": 0,
          "explain": "מִצְוָה, commandment, ends in ָה, the usual feminine ending."
        },
        {
          "type": "match",
          "letters": true,
          "prompt": "Match each ending to what it means.",
          "pairs": [["-ִים", "more than one (masculine)"], ["-וֹת", "more than one (feminine)"], ["-ַיִם", "a pair"], ["-ָה", "one (feminine)"]]
        },
        {
          "type": "parse",
          "prompt": "Describe מְלָכִים.",
          "word": "מְלָכִים",
          "fields": [
            { "label": "Gender", "options": ["masculine", "feminine"], "answer": "masculine" },
            { "label": "How many?", "options": ["one", "more than one", "a pair"], "answer": "more than one" }
          ],
          "explain": "מְלָכִים, kings: the plural of מֶלֶךְ, with the vowels changed and -ִים added."
        },
        {
          "type": "parse",
          "prompt": "Describe בָּנוֹת.",
          "word": "בָּנוֹת",
          "fields": [
            { "label": "Gender", "options": ["masculine", "feminine"], "answer": "feminine" },
            { "label": "How many?", "options": ["one", "more than one", "a pair"], "answer": "more than one" }
          ],
          "explain": "בָּנוֹת, daughters: the feminine plural ending -וֹת."
        },
        {
          "type": "choose",
          "prompt": "שָׁנָה (year) is feminine. What is its plural?",
          "fragments": true,
          "options": ["שָׁנִים", "שָׁנוֹת", "שָׁנָה"],
          "answer": 0,
          "explain": "שָׁנִים: one of the feminine nouns that takes the masculine ending."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "read",
      "intro": "Find the plural endings.",
      "cards": [
        { "type": "verse", "ref": "GEN 1:14", "note": "At the end, וּלְיָמִים וְשָׁנִים: “and for days and years”, two -ִים plurals." },
        { "type": "verse", "ref": "GEN 1:10", "note": "יַמִּים, “seas”, is the plural of יָם; and הַמַּיִם, “the waters”, ends in -ַיִם." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "review",
      "cards": [
        {
          "type": "words",
          "items": [
            { "k": "H0802H", "t": "אִשָּׁה", "say": "i-SHAH", "en": "woman, wife" },
            { "k": "H1323G", "t": "בַּת", "say": "bat", "en": "daughter" },
            { "k": "H5869A", "t": "עַיִן", "say": "A-yin", "en": "eye; spring" },
            { "k": "H3548", "t": "כֹּהֵן", "say": "ko-HEN", "en": "priest" },
            { "k": "H5030", "t": "נָבִיא", "say": "na-VI", "en": "prophet" },
            { "k": "H1004B", "t": "בַּיִת", "say": "BA-yit", "en": "house" },
            { "k": "H0127G", "t": "אֲדָמָה", "say": "a-da-MAH", "en": "ground, land" },
            { "k": "H0120G", "t": "אָדָם", "say": "a-DAM", "en": "man, mankind; Adam" },
            { "k": "H4687", "t": "מִצְוָה", "say": "mits-VAH", "en": "commandment" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
